  "id": "landmine-squat-to-press",
  "name": "Landmine Squat to Press",
  "definition": "A standing power repetition using an Olympic bar anchored in a ground landmine. Both hands begin stacked on the moving sleeve at the upper sternum. A near-parallel squat flows into rapid hip, knee, and ankle extension that drives the sleeve forward and upward; the lower hand releases and the other arm finishes the diagonal press. The pressing arm alternates on successive repetitions. NSCA Coach 7.3 specifies this hand change and permits a forward step if needed; this catalog fixture retains a planted-foot finish for consistent tracking. Shoulder and elbow actions and categorical muscle roles are anatomy-and-mechanics inferences, not measured muscle-force rankings. A two-hand finish, strict standing press, free-bar thruster, rotational punch, or second dip is outside this family. Enter added plates only; compare loads only on the same bar and pivot setup.",
